Package: cpueTargeting
Title: Simulators and Tools for CPUE Targeting and Standardization
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("Henning", "Winker", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "henning.winker@fao.org")
Description: Multispecies operating models for exploring spatial and
    vertical targeting and catch-per-unit-effort standardization. Includes
    the multi-habitat cluster example of Winker et al. (2014), the
    four-species bathymetric Run 22 model based on the spatial simulator of
    Thorson et al. (2017) <doi:10.1139/cjfas-2015-0598> and Ono et al. (2015)
    <doi:10.1016/j.fishres.2015.05.021>, and its extension to a longline tuna
    fishery with species vertical distributions and hook depth by
    hooks-between-floats, following the habitat-based approach of Bigelow et
    al. (2002). Provides a step-by-step toolbox for real catch and effort
    data: data formatting, cumulative species curves, fleet and catch
    composition exploration, habitat-based subsetting (Stephens and MacCall
    2004), and targeting covariates from the catch composition (principal
    components with the Optimal Coordinates test, and clustering into
    fishing tactics).
